/E (The study presents a modified influence function approach for predicting ground subsidence associated with underground coal mining. By incorporating the effects of panel geometry, edge influence, subsidence asymmetry, and overlying goaf, the method provides a more realistic representation of observed ground movement in Indian coalfields.)
